    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Robert Rodriguez's Desperado (1995) revolutionized Latino action cinema, blending Mexican mariachi culture with Hong Kong-style gunplay choreography. Following his micro-budget debut <a href=\"/movie/9367\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9367\">El Mariachi</a> (1992), Rodriguez crafted a stylish revenge thriller that launched Antonio Banderas into Hollywood stardom. The film's influence echoes through later works like <a href=\"/movie/1428\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1428\">Once Upon a Time in Mexico</a> (2003) and <a href=\"/movie/23631\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"23631\">Machete</a> (2010), establishing a distinct visual language that combines practical effects with operatic violence."
      },
