      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The mid-90s saw a surge in stylized action cinema, with Desperado emerging alongside genre-defining works like <a href=\"/movie/101\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"101\">The Professional</a> (1994) and <a href=\"/movie/9737\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9737\">Bad Boys</a> (1995). Rodriguez's innovative camera techniques - including the \"gun POV\" shots and dynamic tracking sequences - influenced countless action films that followed. The partnership between Rodriguez and frequent collaborator Quentin Tarantino would continue to shape independent genre filmmaking through the decade."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's technical achievements belie its modest $7 million budget. Rodriguez's \"Mariachi-style\" filmmaking approach - serving as his own director of photography, editor, and sound designer - created a template for independent action cinema. This influenced later directors like <a href=\"/movie/187\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"187\">Sin City</a> (2005) and proved you could achieve Hollywood production value without studio-level budgets. SUBHEAD: Impact on Action Cinema Language"
      },
